      "message": "This wipes out the entire identity table prior to loading anything into it. What happens if a migration is run twice?\n\n\n    1.) user table contains users A, B, and C\n    2.) migration wipes identity table\n    3.) migration moves users A, B, and C to identity table\n    4.) users A and B are modified and the changes are persisted in the identity table\n    5.) a new user is added to the identity able, call it D\n    6.) something terrible happens\n    7.) We run this migration again, losing user D and the changes to A and B\n\nIs that something we can hit?",
